title: Extract as Molecule(s)
manual: write/

Cut a finite piece of the current system and load it as one or more new molecular
systems. Choose a region (a sphere, a cube or a block of unit cells), decide how the
molecules crossing its boundary are treated and, in molecular systems, whether the atoms
are extracted as a single molecule or split into monomers, dimers and higher n-mers. The
number of atoms the region contains is shown next to the "Extract" button.

# Options
- Shape: "Sphere" or "Cube" around a center, or whole "Unit cell" blocks (crystals only).
- Center (Å or frac): the center of the region. "Pick" takes it from the view: click an
  atom to use its position, or empty space to use the clicked point.
- Radius (Å) / Half-edge (Å): the size of the sphere or cube.
- Cells: the number of cells along a, b and c, and "Include border atoms" to keep the atoms
  near the boundary of the chosen cells.
- Extract (molecular systems): "Single molecule" loads the region as one system;
  "Monomers, dimers, etc." splits it into separate n-mers.
- Include: for a single molecule, extract only the "Atoms in the region" (molecules at the
  boundary are left incomplete), "Whole molecules with any atom in the region" (completed
  with atoms from outside) or "Whole molecules centered in the region" (center of mass
  inside).
- Up to n =: the highest n-mer order. For each order, the table sets whether it is
  written, the center-of-mass "Distances" filter and its "Cutoff (Å)", and the "Number
  ('any')" of molecules of the type that must appear; the estimated number of n-mers is
  shown.
- Close after extracting: close the window and select the new system in the view when
  the extraction is done.

# Results
The new systems are added to the tree, one per molecule or n-mer. While the window is
open, the region is drawn in the view so its position and size can be checked.
